# Modules allowed to name the node backend (tools/node_confinement_check.sh).
# One per line: <path from the repository root>: <why it must>.
# A spec is exempt only as a backend's own test: "<spec path>: own test of
# <backend session or adapter module path> — <why>"; it must name what that
# module defines.
offchain/lib/Singular/Provider/Koios/Client.hs: Koios backend — implements submission of signed transactions as CBOR for provider composition; never imported by commands
offchain/lib/Singular/Provider/Koios/Provider.hs: composition — supplies the signed-only write capability through the existing Koios Client.submitTx raw submitter; allowed by the epic new-backend confinement ruling, with no unsigned submission or node route exposed to commands
offchain/devnet/Devnet/Probe.hs: composition — the devnet probe reads a node's raw ledger snapshot and its UTxO by output reference, which the read interface does not answer, over its own node-to-client connection
offchain/e2e-test/Singular/Registry/E2E/NodeSpec.hs: own test of offchain/private-facade/Singular/Registry/Private/RawFacts.hs — independent private ledger facts and wrong-magic probe; generic HTTP wallet/confirmation legs remain separately attributed
conformance/app/Conformance/Run/Node.hs: composition — starts only the private devnet facade and reads its independent private raw facts; supplies shipping HTTP capabilities and an explicit caller wallet to rows
conformance/app/Conformance/Run/Replay.hs: composition — replays a refused submission with traced validators: wraps the raw submitter so each refusal is captured before the next submission, and reads the refused transaction's inputs by output reference, the protocol parameters and the era history over node-to-client, which the read interface does not answer
